    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted as `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the owner's `registrationDate` year.\n\nSince the value is derived entirely from the owner's own fields (`customerCode` + `registrationDate`), I computed it at read time in the mapper \u2014 matching the existing pattern used for the other read-only derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`) rather than persisting a redundant column.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `customerCode`), so the OpenAPI generator adds it to the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `membershipNumber` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a `@Named(\"formatMembershipNumber\")` method that builds `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`. It returns `null` when either source field is absent (consistent with the spec and null-safety of the sibling formatters). The `%02d` guarantees the two-digit, zero-padded year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreMembershipNumberFormat`, which reads the owner back and asserts `customerCode + \"-M\" + YY == membershipNumber`, passes.",
